      "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/news/culture/ancient-civilization-millions-once-flourished-amazon",
      "https://www.newscientist.com/article/2582152-lost-civilisation-in-the-amazon-may-have-numbered-3-million-people/"
    ],
    "originalSource": "Nature",
    "researchBrief": "The discovery of over 20,000 geoglyphs in the Amazon, built by the Aquiry civilization, was corroborated by multiple sources. The Nature article [nature.com](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-026-10835-7) provides the most detailed account, including the use of LiDAR technology to uncover these structures. Scientific American [scientificamerican.com](https://www.scientificamerican.com/article/hundreds-of-ancient-never-before-seen-earthworks-discovered-in-the-amazon/) and the University of Helsinki [helsinki.fi](https://www.helsinki.fi/en/news/culture/ancient-civilization-millions-once-flourished-amazon) confirm the scale of the discovery and the estimated population of 1.25–3 million people. New Scientist [newscientist.com](https://www.newscientist.com/article/2582152-lost-civilisation-in-the-amazon-may-have-numbered-3-million-people/) further supports these findings. The exact number of geoglyphs and the population estimates are based on extrapolations from the data collected, which are consistent across the sources."
